---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <section class="editorial page-width">
    <p class="eyebrow">WHY ZAHARI EXISTS</p>
    <h1>
      Make room
      <br />
      for wonder.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A quieter way to spend time with the things that interest you.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Start with a fortress.</h2>
      <p>
        BTC has a home here: a fortress you can orbit, light and photograph.
        Zahari starts with the art itself, giving you space to explore without
        charts or trading instructions.
      </p>
      <h2>A preview, with room to grow.</h2>
      <p>
        The longer-term idea is a collection of distinct worlds shaped by market
        data and relevant news. This release does not yet connect those sources,
        change the geometry from data, or offer predictions.
      </p>
      <h2>What can I do now?</h2>
      <p>
        Explore the BTC Fortress in 3D, switch between three lighting moods,
        rotate the view and save images to your device. Create an account to use
        your own exploration space.
      </p>
      <h2>Do I need a crypto wallet?</h2>
      <p>
        No. Sign up with a username, password and recovery passcode. There are
        no wallet connections, tokens, purchases or subscriptions in this
        preview.
      </p>
      <a href={Astro.locals.user ? "/studio" : "/signup"} class="button">
        Step inside
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
